Monolithic Architecture is a type of architecture which is developed as an indivisible unit and is deployed as a single unit. Everything is tightly coupled.
The disadvantage here is that any updates in any one of the structure meant deploying the whole application again. It also has a single database. But , it has simple
architecture but gives scalability issues.

Microservice Architecture is kind of loose architecture which helps in scalibility and flexibility. And easy to maintain. 

7)Queue
It is used for handling traffic spikes.“Queues are used to decouple components, absorb traffic spikes, and ensure reliable asynchronous processing.”

8)Push vs Polling
In polling the client asks the same question again and again to the server . But , in push , whenever the server has any message , it is sent to the client.

9)Idempotency
Doing the same thing multiple times gives the same result. Without idempotency , duplicate messages , payment deduction twice.

10) API Gateway
API Gateway , main role is to route traffic to correct server while it can also do tasks like authentication and rate limiting.

11) Load Balancer
It helps in distributing the request to the servers such that one server does not get overloaded. Ensures high availability , scalibility and fault tolerance.

i) Load Balancer -> API gateway , where main focus is upon scalibility and fault tolerance.
ii) API Gateway -> Load Balancer , where main focus is upon authentication , authorization and rate limiting and then there exist different load balancer configurations for different web servers.




